FRAGMENT for .claude/hooks/guard-commit-and-corpus.sh — not a replacement.
PROTOCOL step 4a PROMOTE: a human applies the two lines below and commits.
.claude/hooks/* is protected, so no executor may write it directly (R13).

WHY
---
Two defects, both observed live on 2026-09-08 while orchestrating a wave.

1. A LIVE SUBAGENT BLOCKS EVERY COMMIT ON THE MAIN CHECKOUT.
   The `find "$ROOT" -newer "$STAMP"` at line 26 excludes .git, __pycache__,
   the stamp itself, gate-board.json and two out/ trees. It does NOT exclude
   .claude/worktrees/, where `isolation: worktree` puts a full checkout per
   subagent. Any file a running agent writes is newer than the stamp, so the
   orchestrator is refused:

     BLOCKED: edited after the last regenerate:
       /home/user/obc-interactive/.claude/worktrees/agent-<id>/orchestration/tracks.yaml

   That file is not in the commit, is on a different branch, and is gitignored
   (.gitignore:4). The guard is correct about its own rule and wrong about the
   scope of it. The consequence is structural rather than cosmetic: the wave
   model this project just adopted runs several agents concurrently and gives
   the orchestrator a review gate at each boundary — and under this hook the
   orchestrator cannot commit anything at all while a wave is in flight.

2. RUNNING GATE E1 DISARMS COMMITTING.
   ci/test_hooks.sh:128 ends with `rm -f .regen.stamp`, and must — line 39
   tests that this hook blocks when the stamp is absent, so the suite has to be
   able to remove it. So every local verification sweep leaves the tree in the
   state this hook refuses. Recorded in AUDIT-rev14.md; the fix belongs here.

Neither guard is wrong in isolation. They are wrong about each other.

THE PATCH
---------
Line 26-27, add one exclusion for subagent worktrees:

-  NEWER=$(find "$ROOT" -type f -newer "$STAMP" ! -path '*/.git/*' ! -path '*/__pycache__/*' ! -name '.regen.stamp' \
-          ! -name 'gate-board.json' ! -path '*/verify/*/out/*' ! -path '*/pipeline/emitters/out/*' 2>/dev/null | head -3 | tr '\n' ' ')
+  # .claude/worktrees/ holds a full checkout per subagent (isolation: worktree)
+  # and is gitignored. A running agent's writes are newer than the stamp but are
+  # on another branch and never in this commit, so without this exclusion any
+  # live wave refuses every commit on the main checkout.
+  NEWER=$(find "$ROOT" -type f -newer "$STAMP" ! -path '*/.git/*' ! -path '*/__pycache__/*' ! -name '.regen.stamp' \
+          ! -path '*/.claude/worktrees/*' \
+          ! -name 'gate-board.json' ! -path '*/verify/*/out/*' ! -path '*/pipeline/emitters/out/*' 2>/dev/null | head -3 | tr '\n' ' ')

DEFECT 2 IS NOT PATCHED HERE, DELIBERATELY
-------------------------------------------
Restoring the stamp inside test_hooks.sh would make E1 leave state behind it did
not find, and having this hook distinguish "no stamp" from "stamp older than a
generated file" is a behaviour change to a guard, not a scope fix. Both belong
with the no-data path already proposed for this hook (AUDIT-rev14 WHAT BROKE 3),
where a data-less clone can commit when no generated artifact is in the diff.
Proposed together, applied together, with a control each.

NEW E1 CASES OWED WHEN THIS IS PROMOTED (ci/test_hooks.sh is protected too)
  - a file under .claude/worktrees/ newer than the stamp -> commit PERMITTED
  - a file in the repo proper newer than the stamp       -> commit BLOCKED
The second is the control: without it the exclusion could be widened to
everything and the suite would still pass.

OBSERVED TWICE, MINUTES APART, AND THE RACE IS UNWINNABLE
---------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-08T18:49  BLOCKED on .claude/worktrees/agent-<A>/orchestration/tracks.yaml
2026-09-08T18:51  stamp refreshed at 18:51:30, staged, commit attempted
                  BLOCKED on .claude/worktrees/agent-<A>/tools/fixtures/.gitignore

The second attempt is the important one. `touch .regen.stamp` immediately before
`git commit` makes the stamp newer than every file that exists at that instant -
and it still failed, because a live agent wrote a new file in the gap. There is
no ordering of touch-and-commit that wins against an agent that is still working.

So this is not "an inconvenience the orchestrator can time around". While any
subagent is running, commits on the main checkout are refused, full stop. The
only remedies without this patch are to serialise every wave down to one agent,
or to wait for the whole wave before committing anything - both of which give up
the property the wave model exists to provide.

Note also which file blocked the second attempt: `tools/fixtures/.gitignore`, a
file the agent created seconds earlier inside a gitignored worktree. Nothing
about it is related to whether this repository's generated documentation is
stale, which is the only thing this check is for.
